<poml>
    <task>
        Take robot data from a Bagel source to a certified training dataset: cut the
        moments that matter into a LeRobot export, submit it to a Gantry Bench instance
        for evaluation, and bring the verdict's evidence back into this conversation.
        <stepwise-instructions>
            <list listStyle="decimal">
                <item>
                    Ask the user (if not already stated): which event windows to keep,
                    which Gantry Bench instance to submit to (the api_url, e.g. their
                    deployment's base URL), and what to name the submission.
                </item>
                <item>
                    Cut and export: author a Bagel reduction pipeline whose detection
                    matches the user's event description, with a LeRobot dataset as the
                    output. Preview it before running, as pipelines always are.
                </item>
                <item>
                    Submit: add the submit/gantry_bench task to the pipeline with the
                    LeRobot output as its source, or run it once standalone. The task
                    zips the export, creates the submission, uploads, and writes a
                    receipt artifact with the submission id and report URL. Show the
                    user the receipt.
                </item>
                <item>
                    The bench runs its free gates (intake, then the data report) on its
                    own. Poll GET {api_url}/api/submissions/{id} until g0 and g1 leave
                    "queued"/"running", then relay each gate's one-line verdict. Deeper
                    gates (the signal check, the robot test) cost compute and are the
                    owner's decision: report that they are waiting, do not start them
                    unless the user explicitly asks.
                </item>
                <item>
                    Close the loop: once gates have finished, download
                    {api_url}/api/submissions/{id}/evidence, unzip it, and point Bagel
                    at the directory -- it resolves as the gantry.evidence data source.
                    Offer to run the describe/gantry_verdict capability on it, so the
                    verdict the user just earned is interrogated with the same
                    auditable SQL the rest of Bagel practices.
                </item>
            </list>
        </stepwise-instructions>
        Honesty rules: never present an upload as a verdict -- a submission that has
        only passed intake has been read, not evaluated. Quote gate summaries verbatim
        rather than paraphrasing them into stronger claims, and if a gate refuses or
        abstains, relay the refusal and its reason as the result, because on this bench
        a refusal is a result.
    </task>

    <output-format>
        Keep the user oriented with a short status line after each step: what was cut,
        what was uploaded (name, size, submission id, report URL), what each finished
        gate concluded, and where the evidence bundle landed. Every number quoted from
        the evidence must come from a SQL query shown beside it.
    </output-format>
</poml>
